    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nA line containing U+2028 (LINE SEPARATOR) produces stale or duplicated characters when Neovim scrolls horizontally.\n\n<img width=\"211\" height=\"83\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2dd7c162-2c4a-467e-9570-4e198e4e4a11\" />\n\n**Additional context**:\n\nI initially reported this to Ghostty:\nhttps://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty/discussions/14821\n\nA Ghostty collaborator identified a width disagreement: Ghostty treats U+2028 as width 0, while Neovim treats it as width 1. They suggested that Neovim might classify it as non-printable: https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty/discussions/14821#discussioncomment-19157453\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Run `nvim --clean`.\n2. Set `:set nowrap`.\n3. Resize the terminal to 120 columns.\n4. Enter Insert mode and paste the following text. It contains an actual U+2028 immediately before the second group of words:\n\n   ```text\n   xxxx xxx xxxxxx xxx xxxxxxx xxxx xx+ xxxxx xx xxxxx.  xxx xxxx xxxxxxx xxxxxxx xxxxx, xxx xxx xx xx xxx xxxxx xxxxxxx xxxxxxx xx xxxxxx.²\n   ```\n5. Type `\"` at the end and press Escape.\n\nGhost characters can appear near the end of the line, including apparent copies of `²` or other stale glyphs. The window width matters: the issue does not reproduce at every width.\nReplacing U+2028 with an ordinary space prevents the issue in my tests.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe displayed text should remain correct during horizontal scrolling, without stale or duplicated glyphs.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.12.6\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nseems less frequent in vim, v9.1\n\n### Operating system/version\n\n26.6.2 \n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nghostty 1.3..1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nhomebrew",
